  "goodToKnow": "Homosexuell is the neutral, formal adjective: homosexuelle Paare, die Rechte Homosexueller. In everyday speech, people say schwul (gay, for men) and lesbisch (for women), and many gay men use schwul proudly, though it's also been used as an insult, so tone matters. Germany opened marriage to same-sex couples (Ehe für alle) in October 2017. Before 1994, Paragraph 175 of the criminal code outlawed sex between men."
